; Stage 15 W4b sibling sweep (design/stage15-stress-test/diagnostics.md
; §W4b): the worst sibling found -- before the fix, a bare colon-typed
; struct name ("S:i32") sailed past `emit-defstruct`'s `!= NODE-SYM` check
; unchanged, registered a StructDef under that literal spelling, and then
; failed downstream at `check-ir-name-legal` with a confusing "illegal
; character ':'" message reported at line 0 (S:i32 is an interned NODE-SYM,
; whose own `line` is always 0). Now rejected at the `defstruct` line with a
; message that names the actual mistake.
(defstruct S:i32 (f i32))

(defn main ():i32 0)
